Cloakfox: spoof CSS system-font resolution to match the persona's OS.

Two sibling hooks that stop the REAL host OS leaking through CSS font
resolution even when navigator.platform is spoofed:

1. gfxPlatformFontList::GetSystemUIFontFamilies() — the CSS `system-ui`
   generic. Without this it resolves to the host's UI font (SF/Helvetica on
   macOS, Segoe UI on Windows, Cantarell/DejaVu on Linux). getComputedStyle()
   preserves the "system-ui" keyword, so the leak is via rendered METRICS:
   measuring text in system-ui and comparing against known faces identifies
   the host.

2. gfxMacPlatformFontList::LookupSystemFont() — the CSS2 system-font keywords
   (font: caption | icon | menu | message-box | small-caption | status-bar).
   The Mac build hardcodes "-apple-system" here, which CreepJS's GeckoFonts
   map attributes to macOS — a direct getComputedStyle().fontFamily leak.
   CreepJS probes all six keywords.

Both resolve through CloakfoxPersonaUIFont(), which reads navigator.platform
from the per-container MaskConfig overlay (per-call, so it follows the
container's persona rather than being frozen process-wide) and maps
win->Segoe UI, mac->Helvetica, linux->DejaVu Sans. All three ship in the
bundled font pack (bundle/fonts/), so they resolve on any host. With no
persona active the native defaults are kept.

The Objective-C++ file can't include MaskConfig.hpp — nlohmann/json needs
exceptions, which are disabled for ObjC++ in gfx/thebes — so the lookup lives
in gfxPlatformFontList.cpp and is exported as CloakfoxSystemFontName().

Adapted from Camoufox's system-ui-font-spoofing.patch and
font-system-fonts-css2.patch; extended to cover Linux personas and to read
per-container instead of caching in a process-global static.

